   "subject": "Re: qt4/qt5 and qtpaint package on Ubuntu",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">After installing<div><pre style=\"padding:5px;overflow:auto;width:auto;max-height:600px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;word-wrap:normal;color:rgb(17,17,17);background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\">sudo apt-get install qtbase5-dev</code></pre></div><div>I have reinstalled all the packages, without problem.</div><div>But now I get another error :</div><div><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;;outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:16px;color:rgb(255,255,255);font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important;background-color:rgb(0,34,64)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(255,157,0);white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:rgb(255,157,0)\">library(cranvas)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(255,98,140)\">Error : .onLoad a échoué dans loadNamespace() pour &#39;qtbase&#39;, détails :\r\n  appel : fun(libname, pkgname)\r\n  erreur : FATAL: This application failed to start because it could not find or load the Qt platform plugin &quot;xcb&quot;.\r\n\r\nReinstalling the application may fix this problem.</span></pre></div><div>I have spent some time with Google to install this plugin, but I&#39;m totally lost...</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "8UGqsrRCCAAJ",
   "from": "Xiaoyue Cheng",
   "author": "a5200fbd6eeaa536",
   "date": "2015-12-22T16:21:25Z",
   "subject": "Re: qt4/qt5 and qtpaint package on Ubuntu",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Here is the answer to the very last question:<br><br>&quot;group&quot; is not an argument for qtime any more. You can use vdiv=... for vertical faceting (pressing key V) or hdiv=... for horizontal faceting (pressing key H).</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
